    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0120" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2793: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-26T20:00:00+01:00"
                            >November 26, 1918—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3207. I learn that the French Minister is indignant at the activities of the
                    British Red Cross delegate as reported in my 3190, November 24, 11 p.m., and
                    3204, November 26, 7 [<hi rendition="#italic">5?</hi>] p.m., maintaining that
                    negotiations relative to the armistice conditions should be carried on through
                    Marshal Foch alone and has so telegraphed his Government.</p>
                <p>Copy to London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
